1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,130
[SITARA] Simply put,

2
00:00:01,760 --> 00:00:03,680
you and Emperor Ögedei
have filled me

3
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:05,010
with a sense of hope.

4
00:00:05,090 --> 00:00:06,100
[Boraqchin gasps]

5
00:00:06,390 --> 00:00:07,760
[SITARA] The great wisdom
you both display

6
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:09,430
makes you worthy
of ruling this world

7
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:11,430
with honor and grace. Yes.

8
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:13,770
[tearfully]
Do you really think so?

9
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:16,060
Of course I do.

10
00:00:16,610 --> 00:00:19,820
[BORAQCHIN] There's no need
for you to feel so nervous.

11
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:23,950
I just have something
I wanted to discuss with you.

12
00:00:28,370 --> 00:00:29,450
♪

13
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:32,330
-[indistinct chatter]
-[grunting]

14
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,630
♪

15
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:39,920
[ILÜGE] Good tidings,
Great Kha'an.

16
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,970
Tolui has crossed the Han River.

17
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:44,880
And the enemy troops
have begun scurrying southward.

18
00:00:46,090 --> 00:00:48,550
Tolui, you've done well.

19
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:54,440
All right, let's make our move,
and cross the river ahead.

20
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:57,690
[♪ opening theme song playing]

21
00:02:25,030 --> 00:02:27,740
So, my brother has crossed
the Yellow River?

22
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:31,070
Yes. Reinforcements from
the Great Kha'an are coming.

23
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:32,280
We should muster.

24
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:34,490
That does seem wise.

25
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:36,580
Well, do you know
of a good location?

26
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:38,910
[SUBUTAI] Mount Sanfeng
will serve us well.

27
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,170
♪

28
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:51,390
[SITARA (ADULT)] 130 kilometers
from Kaifeng, the Jin capital.

29
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:54,760
Tolui's army began positioning
themselves

30
00:02:54,850 --> 00:02:56,430
at the foot of Mount Sanfeng,

31
00:02:57,520 --> 00:03:00,230
awaiting the arrival
of reinforcements.

32
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:05,570
Though, the opposing Jin army
seemed ready

33
00:03:05,650 --> 00:03:08,070
to confront them and wage war.

34
00:03:08,150 --> 00:03:09,110
[Wanyan exhales]

35
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:11,950
[WANYAN] You bring orders
to launch an attack now?

36
00:03:12,030 --> 00:03:14,450
My men are thoroughly exhausted.

37
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:16,410
I'm sure our enemy is as well.

38
00:03:16,790 --> 00:03:18,160
The bulk of their main force

39
00:03:18,250 --> 00:03:19,540
has its sights set
on the capital.

40
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:21,710
[Wanyan gasps, grunts]

41
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:25,460
Do away with their troops
at once.

42
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:26,840
[cart rattling]

43
00:03:27,590 --> 00:03:29,220
What shall we do?

44
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:30,800
Follow his orders.

45
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:33,180
Fortunately,
we outnumber the enemy.

46
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:35,390
So, we'll encircle them all.

47
00:03:38,470 --> 00:03:39,640
[Tolui sighs]

48
00:03:39,730 --> 00:03:41,730
They have us
completely surrounded.

49
00:03:41,810 --> 00:03:45,150
There are 150,000 troops,
at least.

50
00:03:45,230 --> 00:03:47,570
Oh, really? And our count?

51
00:03:48,070 --> 00:03:49,860
Under 40,000.

52
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:51,450
-[laughs]
-Uh?

53
00:03:51,530 --> 00:03:53,070
It is no laughing matter, sir.

54
00:03:53,160 --> 00:03:54,530
If the Great Kha'an's
reinforcements

55
00:03:54,620 --> 00:03:56,280
don't make it in time,
we're done for.

56
00:03:56,370 --> 00:03:58,370
They will, so there's no need
for concern.

57
00:03:58,450 --> 00:04:00,540
-[all groaning]
-[neighs]

58
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:02,000
[commander sighs]

59
00:04:02,660 --> 00:04:04,830
Fine. Then...

60
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:08,130
how about we entrust
our fate to Tengri?

61
00:04:09,590 --> 00:04:10,760
What?

62
00:04:11,050 --> 00:04:13,720
Hmm. Bring me a soldier
who can perform

63
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:15,140
the jadamishi rite.

64
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:26,860
[COMMANDER]
The jadamishi is known

65
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:28,820
to summon storms, isn't it?

66
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:31,990
What is it he hopes to
accomplish by doing this rite?

67
00:04:32,070 --> 00:04:33,070
[Subutai sighs]

68
00:04:33,150 --> 00:04:35,740
♪

69
00:04:55,930 --> 00:04:58,640
[squawking]

70
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:19,910
[all gasp softly]

71
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:23,910
-Now it's...
-Snowing.

72
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,210
And the wind's picked up.

73
00:05:25,290 --> 00:05:26,290
♪

74
00:05:29,170 --> 00:05:30,550
Tengri...

75
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:33,670
So you have agreed
to grant our wish.

76
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:35,510
[footsteps]

77
00:05:35,590 --> 00:05:37,340
[TOLUI] Listen up, men!

78
00:05:38,340 --> 00:05:41,060
Start digging trenches at once!

79
00:05:42,010 --> 00:05:44,350
Have all the men
and horses take cover

80
00:05:44,430 --> 00:05:46,310
before the storm arrives!

81
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:49,360
Cover those horses in blankets.

82
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:52,070
Our soldiers need to be
bundled up!

83
00:05:52,150 --> 00:05:54,150
[wind howling]

84
00:05:55,030 --> 00:05:58,240
[SITARA (ADULT)] The storm raged
for three days and nights.

85
00:05:58,320 --> 00:05:59,450
[grunting]

86
00:05:59,530 --> 00:06:01,120
[SITARA (ADULT)]
Swaying the fates

87
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:04,410
of the two forces
through perilous weather.

88
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:09,830
And then on the fourth day,

89
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:13,000
the 150,000 strong Jin army...

90
00:06:13,090 --> 00:06:14,210
[Tolui laughs]

91
00:06:15,010 --> 00:06:17,010
... subjected to cold
and fatigue in their haste...

92
00:06:17,090 --> 00:06:19,340
[continues laughing]

93
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:24,310
[inhales, grunts]

94
00:06:24,390 --> 00:06:27,310
[horses snorting, neighing]

95
00:06:28,310 --> 00:06:29,940
[SITARA (ADULT)]
...found themselves powerless

96
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:31,810
against the Mongol offensive.

97
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:33,570
[Tolui grunts]

98
00:06:35,030 --> 00:06:36,780
Fire!

99
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:42,200
[men grunting]

100
00:06:45,750 --> 00:06:47,580
[SITARA (ADULT)]
And were annihilated.

101
00:06:47,660 --> 00:06:48,870
♪

102
00:06:49,370 --> 00:06:50,710
[men grunting]

103
00:06:56,170 --> 00:06:59,720
We must return...
back to the capital.

104
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:01,470
[grunting]

105
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:04,510
♪

106
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:10,230
Made it just in time.

107
00:07:10,310 --> 00:07:11,440
[Wanyan gasps]

108
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:19,610
Dear Brother!

109
00:07:19,690 --> 00:07:20,950
Tolui.

110
00:07:21,780 --> 00:07:24,700
-You really did it, didn't you?
-I did nothing.

111
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:30,210
It was Tengri
who favored your flag

112
00:07:30,290 --> 00:07:31,540
throughout our battle.

113
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:33,130
[ÖGEDEI] Still...

114
00:07:33,630 --> 00:07:35,960
I'm so blessed that
you're my younger brother.

115
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:37,420
[Tolui gasps softly]

116
00:07:37,750 --> 00:07:38,840
[chuckles]

117
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:43,510
You all right, General?

118
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:46,930
I'm just thinking
about the past.

119
00:07:47,010 --> 00:07:49,180
Back when Genghis Khan
was at war

120
00:07:49,270 --> 00:07:51,060
with the other
steppe tribe leaders,

121
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:53,230
the enemy performed
the jadamishi rite.

122
00:07:55,650 --> 00:07:59,150
But the storm didn't break over
Genghis Khan and his troops.

123
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:01,320
It fell upon the enemy's forces.

124
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:02,650
♪

125
00:08:06,830 --> 00:08:09,410
Now, when I look
at Prince Tolui,

126
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:12,370
-it's almost as if he...
-[COMMANDER] General...

127
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:14,670
Maybe we ought
to leave it at that.

128
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,130
[SUBUTAI] Hm. Forget it.

129
00:08:18,210 --> 00:08:19,460
♪

130
00:08:19,550 --> 00:08:21,590
[SITARA (ADULT)]
After winter had passed,

131
00:08:21,670 --> 00:08:24,010
and spring was at its end,

132
00:08:24,090 --> 00:08:28,180
Ögedei and Tolui set out on
their journey back to Mongolia.

133
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:30,810
Entrusting the capture
of Kaifeng

134
00:08:30,890 --> 00:08:34,190
to their most trusted
veteran generals.

135
00:08:34,270 --> 00:08:37,060
And they were enough
to do the job.

136
00:08:39,650 --> 00:08:42,110
Only two years after this,

137
00:08:42,190 --> 00:08:46,120
the Jin dynasty
would come to an end.

138
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:47,370
♪

139
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:55,460
[TOLUI] At this rate,
we'll be back in no time!

140
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:58,500
Seems the circle hunt strategy
was quite a success.

141
00:08:58,590 --> 00:09:00,210
That right, Boroldai?

142
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:02,420
Name's still Otai, Father.

143
00:09:02,510 --> 00:09:03,470
[TEMÜGE] Hmm.

144
00:09:04,470 --> 00:09:06,630
And while I didn't lose out
in the end,

145
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:08,930
I didn't exactly gain much,
either.

146
00:09:09,010 --> 00:09:10,180
- [laughs]
- [TEMÜGE] I wonder

147
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:12,930
who benefitted the most from it.

148
00:09:16,390 --> 00:09:17,940
♪

149
00:09:19,690 --> 00:09:20,690
[KIRGISTANI] Huh?

150
00:09:27,530 --> 00:09:30,200
Congratulations
on your great victory.

151
00:09:30,780 --> 00:09:31,830
[Ögedei grunts]

152
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:34,120
Glad to see you're looking
so well, Boraqchin.

153
00:09:34,210 --> 00:09:36,080
I have acquired a gift for you.

154
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:37,630
It should be arriving soon.

155
00:09:37,710 --> 00:09:39,380
-I think you'll be pleased.
-Huh?

156
00:09:39,460 --> 00:09:40,420
[BORAQCHIN] Mmm.

157
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:43,340
We've made banquet preparations.
Please come this way.

158
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:46,010
[exclaims] Say, Great Kha'an.

159
00:09:46,090 --> 00:09:48,680
What's this gift?
Is there one for me?

160
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:52,220
-[laughs] Why, of course.
-Oh! What could it be?

161
00:09:52,310 --> 00:09:53,430
[Töregene exhales]

162
00:09:57,270 --> 00:09:58,230
[SITARA] Huh?

163
00:09:58,850 --> 00:10:00,020
[Shira chuckles]

164
00:10:00,110 --> 00:10:01,520
Shira!

165
00:10:05,950 --> 00:10:07,240
Hey, it's been a while.

166
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:08,780
What are you doing here?

167
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:10,830
I'm going to be serving
Prince Tolui for a bit.

168
00:10:10,910 --> 00:10:12,580
Princess's orders.

169
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:14,410
♪

170
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:16,460
[indistinct chatter, laughter]

171
00:10:24,130 --> 00:10:26,880
So, brother, which land
shall we invade next?

172
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:30,590
I'd prefer to build
a capital first.

173
00:10:32,550 --> 00:10:35,390
-Fatima.
-Yes, my Lady Töregene?

174
00:10:35,470 --> 00:10:37,560
You can take your leave
for the evening.

175
00:10:38,060 --> 00:10:40,980
And when I'm in my tent,
don't disturb me.

176
00:10:41,060 --> 00:10:42,020
[SITARA] Uh?

177
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:53,490
[SITARA] Lady Töregene...

178
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:56,410
doesn't really say much to me
at all anymore.

179
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:59,910
It almost seems like
she's avoiding me.

180
00:11:02,420 --> 00:11:04,630
Now I'm not to disturb her
in her tent.

181
00:11:04,710 --> 00:11:05,590
[gasps]

182
00:11:05,670 --> 00:11:06,750
♪

183
00:11:07,420 --> 00:11:08,720
[Sitara gasps]

184
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:10,470
The Great Kha'an?

185
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:16,140
[SITARA (ADULT)]
Just as Ögedei and Tolui

186
00:11:16,220 --> 00:11:18,930
were returning back
to their own territories,

187
00:11:19,020 --> 00:11:20,770
partway through...

188
00:11:20,850 --> 00:11:22,150
[Ögedei breathes heavily]

189
00:11:22,690 --> 00:11:23,940
Great Kha'an? [gasps]

190
00:11:24,570 --> 00:11:27,480
Great Kha'an! Rein in, men!

191
00:11:27,570 --> 00:11:28,940
Are you in pain? What is it?

192
00:11:29,030 --> 00:11:32,530
Great Kha'an?
Someone fetch a physician!

193
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:33,780
[SITARA (ADULT)]
... Emperor Ögedei

194
00:11:33,870 --> 00:11:36,370
was suddenly struck down
by a mysterious illness.

195
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:44,290
[Kirgistani crying]

196
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:45,710
Great Kha'an!

197
00:11:45,790 --> 00:11:48,380
I'm certain he's just tired
from the long journey.

198
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:49,970
-It will be all right, I'm sure.
-Oh, that poor man!

199
00:11:50,050 --> 00:11:51,970
[Kirgistani continues crying]

200
00:11:52,050 --> 00:11:54,930
[SITARA] What is it?
This ominous feeling.

201
00:11:55,010 --> 00:11:56,720
Something doesn't feel right.

202
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,510
[MÖGE] Slave girl.

203
00:11:59,430 --> 00:12:00,520
Come with me.

204
00:12:02,390 --> 00:12:04,730
It seems the Great Kha'an
was poisoned.

205
00:12:04,810 --> 00:12:06,230
Poisoned?

206
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:08,520
And it's not just
my false belief this time.

207
00:12:08,610 --> 00:12:11,070
-Boraqchin said so herself.
-[breathes shakily]

208
00:12:11,150 --> 00:12:13,030
Listen to me, you are the one

209
00:12:13,110 --> 00:12:15,570
who saved
Mistress Boraqchin's life.

210
00:12:15,660 --> 00:12:18,330
Which is why
I don't want to doubt you.

211
00:12:18,410 --> 00:12:20,080
What do you mean by that?

212
00:12:21,410 --> 00:12:25,250
The Great Kha'an's symptoms
are the same as Boraqchin's.

213
00:12:25,330 --> 00:12:27,340
He was poisoned
with Rahj al-gar.

214
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:29,130
-[Sitara gasps]
-What's more...

215
00:12:29,210 --> 00:12:31,220
The Rahj al-gar
in Boraqchin's possession

216
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:32,720
has suddenly disappeared.

217
00:12:33,050 --> 00:12:36,890
Only a few souls knew about it,
and where it was located.

218
00:12:36,970 --> 00:12:38,430
Lady Möge, I swear

219
00:12:38,510 --> 00:12:40,470
I don't know anything
about what happened!

220
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:42,600
I would never aim to take
the Great Kha'an's life--

221
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:45,020
What a great relief!
It really wasn't you!

222
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:47,020
Huh? But I haven't made
my case yet.

223
00:12:47,110 --> 00:12:49,730
Nah, I wouldn't understand.
It's fine.

224
00:12:49,820 --> 00:12:51,110
But you know...

225
00:12:51,190 --> 00:12:52,950
Though I am not
the brightest person,

226
00:12:53,030 --> 00:12:56,070
I can tell pretty well whether
someone is lying to me or not.

227
00:12:56,530 --> 00:12:57,410
[SITARA] Uh?

228
00:12:57,990 --> 00:12:59,700
Are you lost again?

229
00:12:59,780 --> 00:13:00,830
[SITARA] Hm?

230
00:13:01,330 --> 00:13:02,710
[SITARA] Mm...

231
00:13:02,790 --> 00:13:04,790
[MÖGE] Hey! I can see
the doubt on your face!

232
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:08,040
But still,
if it really wasn't you,

233
00:13:08,130 --> 00:13:10,340
then that would mean
it was Töregene.

234
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:11,630
[Sitara gasps]

235
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:13,840
[breathes uneasily]

236
00:13:14,170 --> 00:13:16,130
[both grunt]

237
00:13:16,220 --> 00:13:17,300
♪

238
00:13:37,990 --> 00:13:39,120
[breathes shakily]

239
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:40,530
[MÖGE] Slave girl.

240
00:13:44,250 --> 00:13:47,040
Töregene turned out to have
the Rahj al-gar.

241
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,420
[gasps]

242
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:50,960
She's being held prisoner
while they investigate.

243
00:13:52,300 --> 00:13:53,380
[SITARA] Lady Töregene...

244
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:57,840
It can't be. How?
Is this some sort of plot?

245
00:13:57,930 --> 00:14:01,760
Listen, slave girl,
I have a favor to ask of you.

246
00:14:02,850 --> 00:14:03,890
[Sitara gasps]

247
00:14:10,190 --> 00:14:11,230
[SITARA] Uh?

248
00:14:11,730 --> 00:14:13,940
Empress Boraqchin's ger?

249
00:14:14,030 --> 00:14:15,190
Go in.

250
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:18,990
Pardon the intrusion. Uh?

251
00:14:19,910 --> 00:14:21,080
[BORAQCHIN] Fatima...

252
00:14:21,830 --> 00:14:23,660
Thank you both for coming.

253
00:14:24,330 --> 00:14:26,080
[Ögedei breathes shakily]

254
00:14:27,660 --> 00:14:30,710
I've requested your presence
for one reason.

255
00:14:30,790 --> 00:14:33,460
I would like for you
to save the Great Kha'an.

256
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:35,340
[SITARA]
What do the physicians say?

257
00:14:35,420 --> 00:14:36,590
Who knows?

258
00:14:37,090 --> 00:14:39,630
Töregene may very well
have conspired with a physician.

259
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:41,680
At the present time,
we can't be certain

260
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:43,810
who is trustworthy or not.

261
00:14:45,140 --> 00:14:47,230
I beg of you. Help him.

262
00:14:56,650 --> 00:14:57,860
[SITARA] His symptoms...

263
00:14:57,950 --> 00:14:59,610
They're the same as yours,

264
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:01,780
when you were poisoned
by Rahj al-gar.

265
00:15:01,870 --> 00:15:04,490
It's safe to assume that
he has been poisoned as well.

266
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:09,160
I've already used
more than half of the stone.

267
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:11,420
If you'll allow,

268
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:14,250
I'll serve you as your
new Jada stone, Highness.

269
00:15:14,880 --> 00:15:18,510
Empress Boraqchin,
may I ask you one thing?

270
00:15:18,590 --> 00:15:21,010
-What is it?
-Lady Töregene...

271
00:15:21,090 --> 00:15:23,220
Why would she want
to poison him?

272
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:26,890
I see. Töregene was
your mistress, wasn't she?

273
00:15:26,970 --> 00:15:29,520
I imagine this comes
as a great shock to you.

274
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:30,770
-However...
-[gasps]

275
00:15:30,850 --> 00:15:33,020
That woman is a complete fool!

276
00:15:33,810 --> 00:15:35,690
She has openly shown resentment

277
00:15:35,770 --> 00:15:38,400
toward the Great Kha'an
time and time again.

278
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:40,360
And upon gaining your wisdom,

279
00:15:40,450 --> 00:15:42,990
she was driven
to commit this foul act.

280
00:15:43,820 --> 00:15:47,330
I'm sure it was her intention
to lay all the blame onto you,

281
00:15:47,410 --> 00:15:49,450
and evade justice herself.

282
00:15:49,540 --> 00:15:51,040
That can't be true!

283
00:15:52,290 --> 00:15:53,460
I don't believe it.

284
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:55,500
How can you be so sure?

285
00:15:55,590 --> 00:15:58,670
Because... she wouldn't do that.

286
00:15:58,750 --> 00:16:01,510
After all, she was willing
to tell me about everything.

287
00:16:02,380 --> 00:16:03,800
Everything...

288
00:16:03,890 --> 00:16:06,300
that she'd kept sealed away
in her heart.

289
00:16:06,890 --> 00:16:09,390
Even of the people
she'd once loved.

290
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:11,890
And the anger
she bears to this day.

291
00:16:11,980 --> 00:16:13,640
Is that really so?

292
00:16:13,730 --> 00:16:15,770
[gasps] Huh?

293
00:16:15,860 --> 00:16:20,320
Fatima, you served Sorghaghtani
before you came here, yes?

294
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:22,450
Töregene is hardly so naive

295
00:16:22,530 --> 00:16:24,450
that she would trust you
as easily as that,

296
00:16:24,530 --> 00:16:26,490
knowing who you
previously served?

297
00:16:26,580 --> 00:16:28,330
Now think back carefully, girl.

298
00:16:28,410 --> 00:16:29,950
Is there anything
she could have done

299
00:16:30,040 --> 00:16:32,040
that you might have found
remotely suspicious?

300
00:16:35,790 --> 00:16:39,000
[SITARA] Did Lady Töregene
really do this?

301
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:42,590
Empress Boraqchin...

302
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:45,130
Please grind up this stone

303
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:48,220
and have the Great Kha'an
take some every day.

304
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:51,930
If you end up running out,
please find another Jada stone.

305
00:16:52,020 --> 00:16:54,480
One with a similar color
to this stone if possible.

306
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:55,600
[both gasp]

307
00:16:56,360 --> 00:16:58,480
-You have my gratitude.
-[chuckles]

308
00:17:05,910 --> 00:17:07,570
[grunts] Brother has fallen ill?

309
00:17:07,660 --> 00:17:10,240
So how is he faring?
Is it curable?

310
00:17:10,330 --> 00:17:12,660
[SHIRA] It is unknown
what disease has befallen him.

311
00:17:12,750 --> 00:17:14,410
But physicians
from east and west

312
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:15,750
have convened to tend to him.

313
00:17:15,830 --> 00:17:18,540
I hear he is already
showing signs of recovery.

314
00:17:18,630 --> 00:17:19,800
Really?

315
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:22,260
Great Khatun Boraqchin
has called for kams

316
00:17:22,340 --> 00:17:23,590
to perform an exorcism.

317
00:17:23,670 --> 00:17:25,880
And asks that you attend
as well, Highness.

318
00:17:25,970 --> 00:17:28,890
-[TOLUI] I'll go at once!
-[gasps] Wait, Tolui!

319
00:17:28,970 --> 00:17:29,970
[TOLUI] Uh?

320
00:17:31,140 --> 00:17:32,520
Sorghaghtani?

321
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:35,850
He suddenly fell ill?
Something doesn't seem right.

322
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:38,980
Shira, what did Fatima say?

323
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:40,520
She told me...

324
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:43,070
There are many
who won't take kindly

325
00:17:43,150 --> 00:17:45,440
to relying solely
on foreign physicians.

326
00:17:45,530 --> 00:17:48,450
Which is why they're adhering
to Mongol tradition

327
00:17:48,530 --> 00:17:50,120
by performing an exorcism.

328
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:52,330
At least, that's what
I have been told.

329
00:17:52,410 --> 00:17:54,000
Well, that makes sense.

330
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:55,790
Tell Princess Sorghaghtani this.

331
00:17:55,870 --> 00:17:56,790
[SHIRA] Huh?

332
00:17:57,580 --> 00:17:59,460
Please do not fret.

333
00:17:59,540 --> 00:18:01,550
Empress Boraqchin
is quite clever,

334
00:18:01,630 --> 00:18:04,710
and she is worthy
of being trusted. [chuckles]

335
00:18:06,510 --> 00:18:07,840
[SORGHAGHTANI] It's true.

336
00:18:07,930 --> 00:18:10,890
I've heard tell of how clever
Boraqchin Khatun is.

337
00:18:10,970 --> 00:18:13,770
You worry too much,
Sorghaghtani.

338
00:18:14,350 --> 00:18:17,480
'Cause after all,
it is merely an exorcism.

339
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:19,810
Tengri has always sided
with my brother

340
00:18:19,900 --> 00:18:21,650
in his past battles.

341
00:18:21,730 --> 00:18:25,190
I'm quite sure...
Tengri will protect him now too.

342
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:26,940
Yes.

343
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:31,070
[Tolui grunts]

344
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:32,200
Oh.

345
00:18:35,490 --> 00:18:37,870
[SORGHAGHTANI]
"It is merely an exorcism."

346
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:39,620
I suppose that's true.

347
00:18:39,710 --> 00:18:41,920
I'll have to put my faith
in Fatima's words.

348
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,800
[indistinct chatter]

349
00:18:51,350 --> 00:18:53,010
[MAN 1]
The Great Kha'an has fallen ill?

350
00:18:53,100 --> 00:18:55,810
I've heard rumors
someone put a curse on him.

351
00:18:55,890 --> 00:18:58,890
Hush! You mustn't speak
so frivolously about curses.

352
00:18:58,980 --> 00:19:01,150
-[chatter continues]
-[SITARA] Lady Töregene...

353
00:19:01,980 --> 00:19:04,570
I wish I could talk to you
right now.

354
00:19:05,190 --> 00:19:09,610
Perhaps this is my best chance,
amidst all this commotion.

355
00:19:09,700 --> 00:19:11,990
[chatter continues indistinctly]

356
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:28,300
[Ögedei breathes heavily]

357
00:19:52,150 --> 00:19:53,570
The malevolent spirits

358
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:56,580
have now been sealed away
in the water within this bowl.

359
00:19:56,660 --> 00:19:58,660
The guardian spirits
have spoken,

360
00:19:58,740 --> 00:20:00,370
and they tell us
that saving the patient

361
00:20:00,450 --> 00:20:02,790
will require a sacrifice
in his stead.

362
00:20:02,870 --> 00:20:05,960
One of you must drink
every last drop of this water.

363
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:07,670
[all gasp]

364
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:12,680
Then allow me to do it.

365
00:20:12,760 --> 00:20:14,140
[Möge gasps]

366
00:20:14,220 --> 00:20:16,640
[BORAQCHIN]
I'm past my prime already.

367
00:20:18,220 --> 00:20:20,220
[KAM] Please wait a moment.

368
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:24,520
A blood relative would make
for a better sacrifice.

369
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:26,190
What now?

370
00:20:26,270 --> 00:20:28,780
A child or grandchild
of the Great Kha'an

371
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:31,650
would certainly suffice.
Or perhaps...

372
00:20:31,740 --> 00:20:33,070
A brother of his?

373
00:20:33,150 --> 00:20:34,570
[all gasp]

374
00:20:38,950 --> 00:20:40,830
Well then, it's me.

375
00:20:41,620 --> 00:20:43,000
Uncle.

376
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:44,250
♪

377
00:21:02,220 --> 00:21:03,980
[TOLUI] Oh, Tengri...

378
00:21:04,810 --> 00:21:06,350
If it is for my brother's sins

379
00:21:06,440 --> 00:21:08,610
that you have made away
with his soul,

380
00:21:08,690 --> 00:21:12,490
then you already know of a soul
with deeper sins than his.

381
00:21:12,570 --> 00:21:15,070
For it is I who have taken
many more lives,

382
00:21:15,150 --> 00:21:17,240
and plundered more than he has.

383
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:23,660
But wait, hold on.

384
00:21:23,750 --> 00:21:25,830
What if he was actually summoned
for his talents,

385
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:28,420
to faithfully serve
at Tengri's side?

386
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:31,130
Well, then.
I'm still the better choice.

387
00:21:31,210 --> 00:21:32,590
[all breathe uneasily]

388
00:21:34,050 --> 00:21:35,340
♪

389
00:21:40,970 --> 00:21:42,970
[Tolui gulping]

390
00:21:50,650 --> 00:21:51,860
[Tolui sighs]

391
00:21:51,940 --> 00:21:52,980
♪

392
00:22:03,740 --> 00:22:06,790
[♪ closing theme song playing]

393
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:35,590
[SITARA (ADULT)]
Next time: "Wisdom."

